OWASP Cheat Sheet: OS Command Injection Defense > Java

This creates a builder with one command-list element, not a program followed by two arguments. `ProcessBuilder` represents the executable and its arguments as a list. The snippet does not start a process or demonstrate shell-command injection.

*Correct Usage:*

This illustrative example starts a process with a modified working directory and passes the executable and each argument separately. Keep the executable and working directory trusted, and validate any untrusted arguments for the invoked program. Argument separation does not replace argument validation.

``` java
ProcessBuilder pb = new ProcessBuilder("TrustedCmd", "TrustedArg1", "TrustedArg2");

Map<String, String> env = pb.environment();

pb.directory(new File("TrustedDir"));

Process p = pb.start();
```

